  "body": "Wanted: the Heidenhain DIN/ISO post writes the smoothing mode in `G62`. Today the post reads `SmoothingMode` (finish or rough) but never writes it. `smoothOn` writes only `G62 T<tol>`, and it does not check T against the upper limit of the tolerance cycle.\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `1c0152c91`):\n- `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps:313`: `smoothMode` is set from `SmoothingMode`.\n- `heidenhain.cps:360-364`: `smoothOn` writes only `G62` and `T`.\n- `heidenhain.cps:369`: `smoothMode` is cleared, and it is never read.\n- HEIDENHAIN TNC 640 ISO programming manual (ID 892909-25), the tolerance cycle (`G62`).\n\nFound by the post audit against the HEIDENHAIN manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means:\n- The post writes the finish or rough mode of `G62` from `SmoothingMode`.\n- The post refuses a T outside the documented range by name.\n- A test pins each one, and a program with no smoothing posts the same output as before.\n",
